A witness for rule A15: a topology record whose budget stops one revision short of the
graph it authorises.

This is the real shape the record was in on 2026-09-02. The revision that added the Android
composition root states what the head composes, why it is an application rather than a
console program, and what it does not settle - and carries no budget paragraph. The last
stated size therefore remained the one before it.

### 2026-08-31 - the JS-1 roots

**The budget.** JS-1 adds two projects and no packable assembly.

The graph goes from 17 projects and 46 edges to 19 and 55. **The packable set is
unchanged at exactly three.**

### 2026-09-02 - a second solution, and a composition root that is an application

**And the first composition root that is an application rather than a console program.**
`Broiler.VM.Composition.JavaScript.Android` composes what the execution-only root composes
and differs by its target framework.

**What it does not settle.** No RID claim moves, and the head's collection is on an
emulator.

**What is not edited.** Every revision above stands as written.
